            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Interesting expansion of this work \ud83d\udc4d\n\nDid not try it out yet but provide some quick feedback."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Mohammed Javith Akthar M",
                        "email": "mohammedjavitham@ami.com",
                        "username": "mohammedjavitham"
                    },
                    "message": "Updated as per the discussion in discord thread"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-evb/meta-evb-arm/meta-evb-fvp-base/README.md",
                    "line": 24,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Maybe it would be better to call it ```Host Console``` and not ```SOL``` since the ```SOL``` is an interface provided by the BMC, right?\n\nThen we can have a separate line connecting the ```/dev/ttyAMA3 ``` in the Base  FVP to an ```\"SOL\"``` label outside to clarify that we are accessing it from outside."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-evb/meta-evb-arm/meta-evb-fvp-base/README.md",
                    "line": 24,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Mohammed Javith Akthar M",
                        "email": "mohammedjavitham@ami.com",
                        "username": "mohammedjavitham"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-evb/meta-evb-arm/meta-evb-fvp-base/recipes-phosphor/console/obmc-console/server.ttyAMA3.conf",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "I expect you want to specify `upstream-tty` here, which relates to the TTY opened for the connection to the host. `local-tty` refers to a TTY to which `obmc-console` mirrors the output from `upstream-tty`, as a software implementation of e.g. Aspeed's UART mux."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-evb/meta-evb-arm/meta-evb-fvp-base/recipes-phosphor/console/obmc-console/server.ttyAMA3.conf",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Mohammed Javith Akthar M",
                        "email": "mohammedjavitham@ami.com",
                        "username": "mohammedjavitham"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-evb/meta-evb-arm/meta-evb-fvp-base/recipes-phosphor/console/obmc-console/server.ttyAMA3.conf",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "This shouldn't be necessary:\n\n```\n> git grep -F '\"default\"'\nconfig.c:#define DEFAULT_CONSOLE_ID \"default\"\n```\n\nFrom there you can follow the use of `DEFAULT_CONSOLE_ID` in the source."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-evb/meta-evb-arm/meta-evb-fvp-base/recipes-phosphor/console/obmc-console/server.ttyAMA3.conf",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Mohammed Javith Akthar M",
                        "email": "mohammedjavitham@ami.com",
                        "username": "mohammedjavitham"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
